{"type":"text","timestamp":1794348526368,"sessionID":"ses_e3881931cffeUV0aIWtfc95zIA","part":{"id":"prt_1c781aaf60018oVP208n16H5xN","messageID":"msg_1c7817411001odo0P9Dk1bqVon","sessionID":"ses_e3881931cffeUV0aIWtfc95zIA","type":"text","text":"<think>The venv creation might be failing due to permissions (ensurepip?). Let me try installing flask into the user site with pip --user, or use a venv in /workspace.\n\nActually maybe the denial is about creating the venv directory in /tmp/opencode (external dir write?). The rule allows /tmp/opencode but denies external_directory... confusing. The error says the tool call was prevented by a rule. Possibly `python3 -m venv venv` writes to ~/.local or something? Hmm.\n\nLet me try a simpler command in /workspace: pip install --user flask.\n\nActually, maybe the issue is that the rule \"external_directory\" with pattern \"*\" action \"ask\" triggers a prompt for paths outside the workspace, and the tool can't ask. /tmp/opencode is explicitly allowed though...\n\nLet me test with a trivial command in/tmp/opencode.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794348526327,"end":1794348526364}}}
