{"type":"text","timestamp":1794348692230,"sessionID":"ses_e3881931cffeUV0aIWtfc95zIA","part":{"id":"prt_1c78432f2001PdObQf1dXdViNx","messageID":"msg_1c78427e20012bhKqAKAEy21V1","sessionID":"ses_e3881931cffeUV0aIWtfc95zIA","type":"text","text":"<think>The server is running (the command hung because of the background job holding the shell, but it completed the important parts). The health check works and data was created.\n\nNote the shell timed out — the background gunicorn keeps the shell open. I need to be careful: use `setsid ... &` with output redirected and `disown`, or run with `nohup ... &` and then `sleep`. The issue is the shell waits for the background process's stdout/stderr? I redirected to a file, so it shouldn't... The tool waits for all child processes maybe. Let me use `setsid` and redirect stdin from /dev/null to fully detach.\n\nThe server is still running now. Let me runthe smoke test.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794348692210,"end":1794348692227}}}
