{"type":"text","timestamp":1794348853425,"sessionID":"ses_e3881931cffeUV0aIWtfc95zIA","part":{"id":"prt_1c786a8a3001EbsXVvsB9CTdVn","messageID":"msg_1c7869e80001DMMjTMrq5SeTbn","sessionID":"ses_e3881931cffeUV0aIWtfc95zIA","type":"text","text":"<think>Now add the `/api/notifications/types` endpoint to the backend.\n\nThen write the components.\n\nBackend endpoint:\n```python\n@app.get(\"/api/notifications/types\")\n@require_user\ndef notification_types():\n    rows = query(\"SELECT DISTINCT type FROM notifications WHERE user_id = ? ORDER BY type\", (g.user[\"id\"],))\n    return jsonify({\"types\": [row[\"type\"] for row in rows]}), 200\n```\n\nRoute ordering: `/api/notifications/types` (static) vs `/api/notifications/<int:notification_id>` — Werkzeug prefers the static rule. But there's a subtlety: `/api/notifications/read-all` is a POST route; a GET to it would 405 vs matching the types route? No, different paths.\n\nLet me add it after read-all.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794348853411,"end":1794348853423}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794348853449,"sessionID":"ses_e3881931cffeUV0aIWtfc95zIA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_01a1c786a529750c9077c19d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/app.py","newString":"@app.get(\"/api/notifications/types\")\n@require_user\ndef notification_types():\n    rows = query(\n        \"SELECT DISTINCT type FROM notifications WHERE user_id = ? ORDER BY type\",\n        (g.user[\"id\"],),\n    )\n    return jsonify({\"types\": [row[\"type\"] for row in rows]}), 200\n\n\n@app.post(\"/api/notifications/read-all\")","oldString":"@app.post(\"/api/notifications/read-all\")"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -264,8 +264,18 @@\n     notification = insert_notification(message, type_.strip(), g.user[\"id\"])\n     return jsonify(notification), 201\n \n \n+@app.get(\"/api/notifications/types\")\n+@require_user\n+def notification_types():\n+    rows = query(\n+        \"SELECT DISTINCT type FROM notifications WHERE user_id = ? ORDER BY type\",\n+        (g.user[\"id\"],),\n+    )\n+    return jsonify({\"types\": [row[\"type\"] for row in rows]}), 200\n+\n+\n @app.post(\"/api/notifications/read-all\")\n @require_user\n def read_all_notifications():\n     cursor = execute(\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/backend/app.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -264,8 +264,18 @@\n     notification = insert_notification(message, type_.strip(), g.user[\"id\"])\n     return jsonify(notification), 201\n \n \n+@app.get(\"/api/notifications/types\")\n+@require_user\n+def notification_types():\n+    rows = query(\n+        \"SELECT DISTINCT type FROM notifications WHERE user_id = ? ORDER BY type\",\n+        (g.user[\"id\"],),\n+    )\n+    return jsonify({\"types\": [row[\"type\"] for row in rows]}), 200\n+\n+\n @app.post(\"/api/notifications/read-all\")\n @require_user\n def read_all_notifications():\n     cursor = execute(\n","additions":10,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"backend/app.py","time":{"start":1794348853419,"end":1794348853432}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c786a8a6001Wvrfc4YI1fQdkL","sessionID":"ses_e3881931cffeUV0aIWtfc95zIA","messageID":"msg_1c7869e80001DMMjTMrq5SeTbn"}}
