{"type":"text","timestamp":1794349030764,"sessionID":"ses_e3881931cffeUV0aIWtfc95zIA","part":{"id":"prt_1c7895d5c001SlYsb5y7067xCC","messageID":"msg_1c78950e5001dKwdonaR8v3zJo","sessionID":"ses_e3881931cffeUV0aIWtfc95zIA","type":"text","text":"<think>The bundle references `process.env.NODE_ENV` → React's dev/prod check. In the IIFE lib build, Vite doesn't replace process.env.NODE_ENV by default in lib mode? Actually Vite defines `process.env.NODE_ENV` in builds... For lib mode it may not. Let me define `window.process = { env: { NODE_ENV: \"production\" } }` in jsdom before injecting the script.\n\nLet me addthat.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794349030749,"end":1794349030761}}}
